            <abstract>
                <para>
                    I/O and CPU scheduling in &sles;&nbsp;Real Time (&slsa;&nbsp;RT) optimizes resource 
                    allocation to ensure deterministic execution for latency-sensitive tasks. By configuring block device 
                    schedulers, assigning process I/O priorities with <literal>ionice</literal> and isolating CPU cores using 
                    &systemd; and <literal>taskset</literal>, administrators prevent disk starvation and latency spikes. 
                    This coordination guarantees predictable response times and maximum system throughput for mission-critical 
                    real-time applications.
                </para>
                <para><emphasis role="bold">Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
                <itemizedlist>
                    <listitem><para>&sles;&nbsp;Real Time installed with the cgroups v2 hierarchy</para></listitem>
                    <listitem><para>Access to a command-line terminal with &systemd;, <literal>taskset</literal>, 
                    <literal>chrt</literal> and <literal>ionice</literal> available</para></listitem>
                </itemizedlist>
            </abstract>
